  "result_text": "Now I have enough information. Based on my verification of the cyhole API, I can write the code:\n\n```python\nfrom cyhole.jupiter import Jupiter\nfrom cyhole.jupiter.client import GetSwapOrderParams, PostSwapExecuteBody\n\n# Initialize Jupiter client\njupiter = Jupiter()\n\n# Define token addresses for Solana\nSOL_ADDRESS = \"So11111111111111111111111111111111111111112\"\nUSDC_ADDRESS = \"EPjFWdd5Au17EggbyWDzjpmbQ3o6xvU9mRREsKpumpw\"\n\n# Step 1: Get a swap quote (order) from SOL to USDC\nquote_params = GetSwapOrderParams(\n    input_mint=SOL_ADDRESS,\n    output_mint=USDC_ADDRESS,\n    amount=1000000,  # 1 SOL in lamports\n    slippage_bps=500,  # 5% slippage tolerance\n)\n\nquote_response = jupiter.client.get_swap_order(quote_params)\nprint(\"Quote Response:\", quote_response)\n\n# Step 2: Execute the swap using the quote\nexecute_body = PostSwapExecuteBody(\n    quote_response=quote_response,\n    user_public_key=\"YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE\",  # Replace with actual wallet public key\n)\n\nexecute_response = jupiter.client.post_swap_execute(execute_body)\nprint(\"Execute Response:\", execute_response)\n```",
